  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Co-Financing support to the World Bank Learning Enhancement and Access Program (LEAP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Government is co-financing the next World Bank International Development Assistance loan program to the education sector in Papua New Guinea. The Program - Learning Enhancement and Access Program (LEAP) &#x2013; is valued at USD100 million and will begin in May 2025. Australia has contributed an additional AUD16 million grant funding.  LEAP is a 10-year multi phased program to be delivered in three phases: Phase 1 will build the foundations for ECE and early primary grades, piloting cost effective ways of delivering ECE, scaling up an existing package of literacy interventions to 4 provinces with some activities having nationwide reach, and making investments in the education management system and in basic infrastructure to align the system towards learning. Phases 2 and 3 will expand the geographic scope and grade range towards reducing poverty. All three phases will center around student learning data to inform key investments and decision-making.</narrative>
  </description>
